    <statement><p>Find the gradient of the given function. Assume the variables
are restricted to a domain on which the function is defined.
<me>f(r,t) = r^{3}\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right).</me></p>
<p><m>\nabla f =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3r^{2}\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\boldsymbol{i}-r^{3}\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\boldsymbol{j}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>f_r = 3r^{2}\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\quad \mbox{and}\quad f_t = -r^{3}\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right),</me>
we have
<me>\nabla f = 3r^{2}\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\boldsymbol{i}-r^{3}\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\boldsymbol{j}.</me>



</solution>
